# SEC Regulation Crowdfunding — 17 CFR Part 227

## Parties and acts

<!-- l4: declare:Actor -->

**1.** In this Act, “Actor” means one of the following—

    (a) “Issuer”;

    (b) “Intermediary”;

    (c) “Investor”; or

    (d) “Purchaser”.

<!-- l4: declare:Action -->

**2.** In this Act, “Action” means one of the following—

    (a) “file a Form C offering statement”;

    (b) “file a Form C-U progress update”;

    (c) “file a Form C-AR annual report”;

    (d) “file a Form C-TR termination of reporting”;

    (e) “advertise the terms of the offering”;

    (f) “transmit funds to the issuer”; or

    (g) “transfer the securities”.

## Thresholds — every dollar figure, bound once, dated per regime

<!-- l4: decide:Reg CF commenced -->

**3.** Reg CF commenced means Date with 16, 5 and 2016.

<!-- l4: decide:the 2017 inflation adjustment -->

**4.** The 2017 inflation adjustment means Date with 12, 4 and 2017.

<!-- l4: decide:the 2021 amendments -->

**5.** The 2021 amendments means Date with 15, 3 and 2021.

<!-- l4: decide:the 2022 inflation adjustment -->

**6.** The 2022 inflation adjustment means Date with 20, 9 and 2022.

<!-- l4: decide:the rules in force include -->

**7.** In relation to a DATE “amendment”, the rules in force include means RULES EFFECTIVE DATE is at least amendment.

<!-- l4: assume:no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16 -->

**8.** In this Act, “no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16” denotes a NUMBER.

<!-- l4: decide:offering maximum in a 12-month period -->

**9.** Offering maximum in a 12-month period means if the rules in force include with the 2021 amendments then 5000000 if the rules in force include with the 2017 inflation adjustment then 1070000 if the rules in force include with Reg CF commenced then 1000000 otherwise no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16.

<!-- l4: decide:income or net worth cut point -->

**10.** Income or net worth cut point means if the rules in force include with the 2022 inflation adjustment then 124000 if the rules in force include with the 2017 inflation adjustment then 107000 if the rules in force include with Reg CF commenced then 100000 otherwise no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16.

<!-- l4: decide:minimum permitted investment -->

**11.** Minimum permitted investment means if the rules in force include with the 2022 inflation adjustment then 2500 if the rules in force include with the 2017 inflation adjustment then 2200 if the rules in force include with Reg CF commenced then 2000 otherwise no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16.

<!-- l4: decide:maximum amount sold to any one investor in a 12-month period -->

**12.** Maximum amount sold to any one investor in a 12-month period means if the rules in force include with the 2022 inflation adjustment then 124000 if the rules in force include with the 2017 inflation adjustment then 107000 if the rules in force include with Reg CF commenced then 100000 otherwise no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16.

<!-- l4: decide:tier 1 ceiling -->

**13.** Tier 1 ceiling means if the rules in force include with the 2022 inflation adjustment then 124000 if the rules in force include with the 2017 inflation adjustment then 107000 if the rules in force include with Reg CF commenced then 100000 otherwise no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16.

<!-- l4: decide:tier 2 ceiling -->

**14.** Tier 2 ceiling means if the rules in force include with the 2022 inflation adjustment then 618000 if the rules in force include with the 2017 inflation adjustment then 535000 if the rules in force include with Reg CF commenced then 500000 otherwise no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16.

<!-- l4: decide:first-time issuer review ceiling -->

**15.** First-time issuer review ceiling means if the rules in force include with the 2022 inflation adjustment then 1235000 if the rules in force include with the 2017 inflation adjustment then 1070000 if the rules in force include with Reg CF commenced then 1000000 otherwise no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16.

<!-- l4: decide:holders of record threshold -->

**16.** Holders of record threshold means 300.

<!-- l4: decide:total assets threshold -->

**17.** Total assets threshold means 10000000.

## Periods — every deadline, bound once

<!-- l4: decide:minimum days publicly available before any sale -->

**18.** Minimum days publicly available before any sale means 21.

<!-- l4: decide:days to file the annual report after fiscal year end -->

**19.** Days to file the annual report after fiscal year end means 120.

<!-- l4: decide:business days to file Form C-TR -->

**20.** Business days to file Form C-TR means 5.

<!-- l4: decide:business days to file a progress update -->

**21.** Business days to file a progress update means 5.

<!-- l4: decide:the resale restriction in years -->

**22.** The resale restriction in years means 1.

# 1. Issuer eligibility — Rule 100(b)

<!-- l4: declare:IssuerProfile -->

**23.** In this Act, “IssuerProfile” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “name”, being a STRING;

    (b) “organized under, and subject to, the laws of a State or territory of the United States or the District of Columbia”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “subject to the requirement to file reports pursuant to section 13 or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “an investment company, or is excluded from the definition of investment company by section 3(b) or section 3(c)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “subject to a disqualification as specified in section 227.503(a)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “has sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) and has not filed the ongoing annual reports required during the two years immediately preceding the filing of the offering statement”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (g) “has no specific business plan, or has indicated that its business plan is to engage in a merger or acquisition with an unidentified company or companies”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: decide:(b)(1) — not organized under State or territorial law -->

**24.** In relation to an IssuerProfile “issuer”, (b)(1) — not organized under State or territorial law if—

    (a) (1); and

    (b) it is not the case that issuer's organized under, and subject to, the laws of a State or territory of the United States or the District of Columbia.

<!-- l4: decide:(b)(2) — an Exchange Act reporting company -->

**25.** In relation to an IssuerProfile “issuer”, (b)(2) — an Exchange Act reporting company if—

    (a) (2); and

    (b) issuer's subject to the requirement to file reports pursuant to section 13 or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act.

<!-- l4: decide:(b)(3) — an investment company -->

**26.** In relation to an IssuerProfile “issuer”, (b)(3) — an investment company if—

    (a) (3); and

    (b) issuer's an investment company, or is excluded from the definition of investment company by section 3(b) or section 3(c).

<!-- l4: decide:(b)(4) — subject to a bad-actor disqualification -->

**27.** In relation to an IssuerProfile “issuer”, (b)(4) — subject to a bad-actor disqualification if—

    (a) (4); and

    (b) issuer's subject to a disqualification as specified in section 227.503(a).

<!-- l4: decide:(b)(5) — delinquent in ongoing annual reports -->

**28.** In relation to an IssuerProfile “issuer”, (b)(5) — delinquent in ongoing annual reports if—

    (a) (5); and

    (b) issuer's has sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) and has not filed the ongoing annual reports required during the two years immediately preceding the filing of the offering statement.

<!-- l4: decide:(b)(6) — no specific business plan, or a blank-check business plan -->

**29.** In relation to an IssuerProfile “issuer”, (b)(6) — no specific business plan, or a blank-check business plan if—

    (a) (6); and

    (b) issuer's has no specific business plan, or has indicated that its business plan is to engage in a merger or acquisition with an unidentified company or companies.

<!-- l4: decide:issuer is excluded by Rule 100(b) -->

**30.** In relation to an IssuerProfile “issuer”, issuer is excluded by Rule 100(b) if—

    (a) (b) Applicability. The crowdfunding exemption shall not apply to transactions involving the offer or sale of securities by any issuer that:;

    (b) (b)(1) — not organized under State or territorial law with issuer;

    (c) (b)(2) — an Exchange Act reporting company with issuer;

    (d) (b)(3) — an investment company with issuer;

    (e) (b)(4) — subject to a bad-actor disqualification with issuer;

    (f) (b)(5) — delinquent in ongoing annual reports with issuer; or

    (g) (b)(6) — no specific business plan, or a blank-check business plan with issuer.

<!-- l4: decide:issuer is eligible -->

**31.** In relation to an IssuerProfile “issuer”, issuer is eligible if issuer is not excluded by Rule 100(b) with issuer.

# 2. Offering limit — Rule 100(a)(1)

<!-- l4: declare:Offering -->

**32.** In this Act, “Offering” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “target offering amount”, being a NUMBER;

    (b) “maximum offering amount the issuer will accept”, being a NUMBER;

    (c) “aggregate amount sold in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months”, being a NUMBER; and

    (d) “the issuer has previously sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6)”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: decide:aggregate offering amount -->

**33.** In relation to an Offering “offering”, aggregate offering amount means the sum of offering's aggregate amount sold in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months and offering's maximum offering amount the issuer will accept.

<!-- l4: decide:offering is within the offering limit -->

**34.** In relation to an Offering “offering”, offering is within the offering limit if—

    (a) (1); and

    (b) aggregate offering amount with offering is at most offering maximum in a 12-month period.

# 3. Investor investment limits — Rule 100(a)(2)

<!-- l4: declare:InvestorProfile -->

**35.** In this Act, “InvestorProfile” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “name”, being a STRING;

    (b) “an accredited investor as defined in Rule 501”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “annual income”, being a NUMBER;

    (d) “net worth”, being a NUMBER; and

    (e) “aggregate amount already sold to this investor across all issuers in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months”, being a NUMBER.

<!-- l4: decide:greater of annual income or net worth -->

**36.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “_self”, greater of annual income or net worth means if _self's annual income is at least _self's net worth, then _self's annual income; otherwise, _self's net worth.

<!-- l4: decide:lesser of annual income or net worth -->

**37.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “_self”, lesser of annual income or net worth means if _self's annual income is at most _self's net worth, then _self's annual income; otherwise, _self's net worth.

<!-- l4: decide:the applicable measure of annual income or net worth -->

**38.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor”, the applicable measure of annual income or net worth means if the rules in force include with the 2021 amendments then investor's greater of annual income or net worth if the rules in force include with Reg CF commenced then investor's lesser of annual income or net worth otherwise no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16.

<!-- l4: decide:either annual income or net worth is less than the cut point -->

**39.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor”, either annual income or net worth is less than the cut point if—

    (a) investor's annual income is less than income or net worth cut point; or

    (b) investor's net worth is less than income or net worth cut point.

<!-- l4: decide:investment limit -->

**40.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor”, investment limit means if either annual income or net worth is less than the cut point with investor, then if minimum permitted investment is at least five percent of the measure, then minimum permitted investment; otherwise, five percent of the measure; otherwise, if ten percent of the measure is at most maximum amount sold to any one investor in a 12-month period, then ten percent of the measure; otherwise, maximum amount sold to any one investor in a 12-month period.

For the purposes of this provision—

“five percent of the measure” means the product of 0.05 and the applicable measure of annual income or net worth with investor;

“ten percent of the measure” means the product of 0.1 and the applicable measure of annual income or net worth with investor;

<!-- l4: decide:aggregate amount sold to this investor including this transaction -->

**41.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor” and a NUMBER “amount to be sold in this transaction”, aggregate amount sold to this investor including this transaction means the sum of investor's aggregate amount already sold to this investor across all issuers in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months and amount to be sold in this transaction.

<!-- l4: decide:the accredited-investor carve-out applies to -->

**42.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor”, the accredited-investor carve-out applies to if—

    (a) the rules in force include with the 2021 amendments; and

    (b) investor's an accredited investor as defined in Rule 501.

<!-- l4: decide:investor is within the investment limit -->

**43.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor” and a NUMBER “amount to be sold in this transaction”, investor is within the investment limit if—

    (a) (2);

    (b) the accredited-investor carve-out applies to with investor; or

    (c) aggregate amount sold to this investor including this transaction with investor and amount to be sold in this transaction is at most investment limit with investor.

# 4. Disclosure requirements — Rules 201, 201(t), 203(a)

<!-- l4: declare:FinancialStatementRequirement -->

**44.** In this Act, “FinancialStatementRequirement” means one of the following—

    (a) “financial statements certified by the principal executive officer, with tax return information”;

    (b) “financial statements reviewed by an independent public accountant”; or

    (c) “financial statements audited by an independent public accountant”.

<!-- l4: assume:the COVID-19 temporary rules, Rule 201(z) and (bb), are not modelled here -->

**45.** In this Act, “the COVID-19 temporary rules, Rule 201(z) and (bb), are not modelled here” denotes a FinancialStatementRequirement.

<!-- l4: decide:the rule date is inside the COVID-19 temporary rules window -->

**46.** The rule date is inside the COVID-19 temporary rules window if—

    (a) RULES EFFECTIVE DATE is at least Date with 4, 5 and 2020; and

    (b) RULES EFFECTIVE DATE is at most Date with 28, 8 and 2022.

<!-- l4: decide:financial statements required -->

**47.** In relation to an Offering “offering”, financial statements required means if the COVID-19 temporary relief could change this answer then the COVID-19 temporary rules, Rule 201(z) and (bb), are not modelled here if aggregate is at most tier 1 ceiling then financial statements certified by the principal executive officer, with tax return information if aggregate is at most tier 2 ceiling then financial statements reviewed by an independent public accountant if first-time issuer relief applies then financial statements reviewed by an independent public accountant otherwise financial statements audited by an independent public accountant.

For the purposes of this provision—

“aggregate” means aggregate offering amount with offering;

“first-time issuer relief applies” means not offering's the issuer has previously sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) and aggregate is at most first-time issuer review ceiling;

“the COVID-19 temporary relief could change this answer” means the rule date is inside the COVID-19 temporary rules window and aggregate is greater than tier 1 ceiling and aggregate is at most 250000;

<!-- l4: decide:assurance level -->

**48.** In relation to a FinancialStatementRequirement “required”, assurance level means consider the case distinctions of required :  when financial statements certified by the principal executive officer, with tax return information has  then 1. when financial statements reviewed by an independent public accountant has  then 2. when financial statements audited by an independent public accountant has  then 3.

<!-- l4: decide:financial statement requirement is satisfied -->

**49.** In relation to an Offering “offering” and a FinancialStatementRequirement “supplied”, financial statement requirement is satisfied means assurance level with supplied is at least assurance level with financial statements required with offering.

<!-- l4: declare:FormCFiling -->

**50.** In this Act, “FormCFiling” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “a Form C offering statement was filed with the Commission and provided to investors and the relevant intermediary prior to the commencement of the offering”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (b) “the Form C includes the information required by section 227.201”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (c) “the financial statements supplied”, being a FinancialStatementRequirement.

<!-- l4: decide:disclosure requirements are met -->

**51.** In relation to a FormCFiling “filing” and an Offering “offering”, disclosure requirements are met if—

    (a) (1);

    (b) filing's a Form C offering statement was filed with the Commission and provided to investors and the relevant intermediary prior to the commencement of the offering;

    (c) filing's the Form C includes the information required by section 227.201; and

    (d) financial statement requirement is satisfied with offering and filing's the financial statements supplied.

# 5. Intermediary obligations — Rules 100(a)(3), 301, 302, 303

<!-- l4: declare:IntermediaryArrangement -->

**52.** In this Act, “IntermediaryArrangement” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “the intermediary complies with section 4A(a) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (b) “the transaction is conducted exclusively through the intermediary's platform”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “the number of intermediaries used for the offering”, being a NUMBER;

    (d) “the intermediary delivered educational materials in connection with establishing the investor's account”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “the intermediary has a reasonable basis for believing that the investor satisfies the investment limitations”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (f) “the days the issuer information has been publicly available on the intermediary's platform before any sale”, being a NUMBER.

<!-- l4: decide:(a)(3) — conducted through a single complying intermediary -->

**53.** In relation to an IntermediaryArrangement “arrangement”, (a)(3) — conducted through a single complying intermediary if—

    (a) (3);

    (b) arrangement's the intermediary complies with section 4A(a) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part;

    (c) arrangement's the transaction is conducted exclusively through the intermediary's platform;

    (d) Instruction to paragraph (a)(3).; and

    (e) arrangement's the number of intermediaries used for the offering is equal to 1.

<!-- l4: decide:the 21-day public availability period has run -->

**54.** In relation to an IntermediaryArrangement “arrangement”, the 21-day public availability period has run if—

    (a) (2); and

    (b) arrangement's the days the issuer information has been publicly available on the intermediary's platform before any sale is at least minimum days publicly available before any sale.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary has discharged its investor-facing duties -->

**55.** In relation to an IntermediaryArrangement “arrangement”, the intermediary has discharged its investor-facing duties if—

    (a) (b) Educational materials. (1);

    (b) arrangement's the intermediary delivered educational materials in connection with establishing the investor's account;

    (c) (b) Investor qualification. (1); and

    (d) arrangement's the intermediary has a reasonable basis for believing that the investor satisfies the investment limitations.

<!-- l4: decide:intermediary obligations are met -->

**56.** In relation to an IntermediaryArrangement “arrangement”, intermediary obligations are met if—

    (a) (a)(3) — conducted through a single complying intermediary with arrangement;

    (b) the 21-day public availability period has run with arrangement; and

    (c) the intermediary has discharged its investor-facing duties with arrangement.

# 6. Advertising restrictions — Rule 204

<!-- l4: declare:AdvertisingNotice -->

**57.** In this Act, “AdvertisingNotice” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “directs investors to the intermediary's platform”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (b) “states that the issuer is conducting an offering pursuant to section 4(a)(6), names the intermediary, and directs the potential investor to its platform”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “states the terms of the offering”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “states factual information about the legal identity and business location of the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (e) “includes information beyond that permitted by paragraph (b)”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: decide:notice complies with Rule 204(b) -->

**58.** In relation to an AdvertisingNotice “notice”, notice complies with Rule 204(b) if—

    (a) (b);

    (b) notice's directs investors to the intermediary's platform;

    (c) (1) A statement that the issuer is conducting an offering pursuant to section 4(a)(6) of the Securities Act, the name of the intermediary through which the offering is being conducted, and information (including a link in any written communications) directing the potential investor to the intermediary's platform;;

    (d) (2) The terms of the offering; and;

    (e) (3) Factual information about the legal identity and business location of the issuer, limited to the name of the issuer of the security, the address, phone number and Web site of the issuer, the email address of a representative of the issuer and a brief description of the business of the issuer.; and

    (f) it is not the case that notice's includes information beyond that permitted by paragraph (b).

<!-- l4: decide:definition — terms of the offering -->

**59.** Definition — terms of the offering if—

    (a) (e) Instruction to section 227.204. For purposes of this section, terms of the offering means the amount of securities offered, the nature of the securities, the price of the securities, the closing date of the offering period, the planned use of proceeds and the issuer's progress toward meeting its funding target.; and

    (b) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:advertising restriction -->

**60.** In relation to an AdvertisingNotice “notice”, advertising restriction means if notice complies with Rule 204(b) with notice, then FULFILLED; otherwise, Issuer must not advertise the terms of the offering..

# 7. Ongoing reporting — Rules 202, 203(b)

<!-- l4: declare:ReportingStatus -->

**61.** In this Act, “ReportingStatus” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “the issuer is required to file reports under section 13(a) or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (b) “annual reports filed since the most recent sale of securities pursuant to this part”, being a NUMBER;

    (c) “holders of record”, being a NUMBER;

    (d) “total assets”, being a NUMBER;

    (e) “the issuer or another party has repurchased all of the securities issued in reliance on section 4(a)(6)”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (f) “the issuer has liquidated or dissolved its business in accordance with state law”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: decide:(b)(1) — became an Exchange Act reporting company -->

**62.** In relation to a ReportingStatus “status”, (b)(1) — became an Exchange Act reporting company if—

    (a) (1); and

    (b) status's the issuer is required to file reports under section 13(a) or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act.

<!-- l4: decide:(b)(2) — one annual report filed and fewer than 300 holders of record -->

**63.** In relation to a ReportingStatus “status”, (b)(2) — one annual report filed and fewer than 300 holders of record if—

    (a) (2);

    (b) status's annual reports filed since the most recent sale of securities pursuant to this part is at least 1; and

    (c) status's holders of record is less than holders of record threshold.

<!-- l4: decide:(b)(3) — three annual reports filed and total assets not exceeding $10,000,000 -->

**64.** In relation to a ReportingStatus “status”, (b)(3) — three annual reports filed and total assets not exceeding $10,000,000 if—

    (a) (3);

    (b) status's annual reports filed since the most recent sale of securities pursuant to this part is at least 3; and

    (c) status's total assets is at most total assets threshold.

<!-- l4: decide:(b)(4) — all securities repurchased -->

**65.** In relation to a ReportingStatus “status”, (b)(4) — all securities repurchased if—

    (a) (4); and

    (b) status's the issuer or another party has repurchased all of the securities issued in reliance on section 4(a)(6).

<!-- l4: decide:(b)(5) — liquidated or dissolved -->

**66.** In relation to a ReportingStatus “status”, (b)(5) — liquidated or dissolved if—

    (a) (5); and

    (b) status's the issuer has liquidated or dissolved its business in accordance with state law.

<!-- l4: decide:ongoing reporting obligation may terminate -->

**67.** In relation to a ReportingStatus “status”, ongoing reporting obligation may terminate if—

    (a) (b) An issuer must continue to comply with the ongoing reporting requirements until one of the following occurs:;

    (b) (b)(1) — became an Exchange Act reporting company with status;

    (c) (b)(2) — one annual report filed and fewer than 300 holders of record with status;

    (d) (b)(3) — three annual reports filed and total assets not exceeding $10,000,000 with status;

    (e) (b)(4) — all securities repurchased with status; or

    (f) (b)(5) — liquidated or dissolved with status.

<!-- l4: decide:ongoing reporting obligation -->

**68.** In relation to a ReportingStatus “status” and a NUMBER “annual cycles”, ongoing reporting obligation means if ongoing reporting obligation may terminate with status, then Issuer must file a Form C-TR termination of reporting, within business days to file Form C-TR.; otherwise, if annual cycles is at most 0, then FULFILLED; otherwise, Issuer must file a Form C-AR annual report, within days to file the annual report after fiscal year end. Upon compliance, ongoing reporting obligation with status and the difference between 1 and annual cycles..

# 8. Resale restrictions — Rule 501

<!-- l4: declare:Transfer -->

**69.** In this Act, “Transfer” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “date the securities were issued”, being a DATE;

    (b) “date of the transfer”, being a DATE;

    (c) “to the issuer of the securities”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “to an accredited investor”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “as part of an offering registered with the Commission”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “to a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “to a trust controlled by the purchaser”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “to a trust created for the benefit of a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (i) “in connection with death of the purchaser”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (j) “in connection with divorce of the purchaser”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (k) “in connection with a circumstance similar to death or divorce of the purchaser”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: decide:days since the securities were issued -->

**70.** In relation to a Transfer “_self”, days since the securities were issued means the difference between Date to days with _self's date the securities were issued and Date to days with _self's date of the transfer.

<!-- l4: decide:the first anniversary of the issuance -->

**71.** In relation to a Transfer “transfer”, the first anniversary of the issuance means add years with transfer's date the securities were issued and the resale restriction in years.

<!-- l4: decide:days until the first anniversary of the issuance -->

**72.** In relation to a Transfer “transfer”, days until the first anniversary of the issuance means the difference between Date to days with transfer's date the securities were issued and Date to days with the first anniversary of the issuance with transfer.

<!-- l4: decide:transfer is within the one-year restricted period -->

**73.** In relation to a Transfer “transfer”, transfer is within the one-year restricted period means transfer's date of the transfer is less than the first anniversary of the issuance with transfer.

<!-- l4: decide:(a)(4) — a family or trust transferee, or a death-or-divorce circumstance -->

**74.** In relation to a Transfer “transfer”, (a)(4) — a family or trust transferee, or a death-or-divorce circumstance if—

    (a) (4);

    (b) To a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent, to a trust controlled by the purchaser, to a trust created for the benefit of a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent,;

    (c) transfer's to a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent;

    (d) transfer's to a trust controlled by the purchaser;

    (e) transfer's to a trust created for the benefit of a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent;

    (f) or in connection with the death or divorce of the purchaser or other similar circumstance.;

    (g) transfer's in connection with death of the purchaser;

    (h) transfer's in connection with divorce of the purchaser; or

    (i) transfer's in connection with a circumstance similar to death or divorce of the purchaser.

<!-- l4: decide:transfer falls within an exception in Rule 501(a) -->

**75.** In relation to a Transfer “transfer”, transfer falls within an exception in Rule 501(a) if—

    (a) unless such securities are transferred:;

    (b) all of the following apply—

        (i) (1); and

        (ii) transfer's to the issuer of the securities;

    (c) all of the following apply—

        (i) (2); and

        (ii) transfer's to an accredited investor;

    (d) all of the following apply—

        (i) (3); and

        (ii) transfer's as part of an offering registered with the Commission; or

    (e) all of the following apply—

        (i) (4); and

        (ii) (a)(4) — a family or trust transferee, or a death-or-divorce circumstance with transfer.

<!-- l4: decide:transfer is permitted -->

**76.** In relation to a Transfer “transfer”, transfer is permitted if—

    (a) transfer is not within the one-year restricted period with transfer; or

    (b) transfer falls within an exception in Rule 501(a) with transfer.

<!-- l4: decide:resale restriction -->

**77.** In relation to a Transfer “transfer”, resale restriction means if transfer falls within an exception in Rule 501(a) with transfer, then FULFILLED; otherwise, Purchaser must not transfer the securities, within days until the first anniversary of the issuance with transfer..

# Top-level — does the transaction qualify for the section 4(a)(6) exemption?

<!-- l4: decide:the transaction qualifies for the section 4(a)(6) exemption -->

**78.** In relation to an IssuerProfile “issuer”, an Offering “offering”, an InvestorProfile “investor”, a NUMBER “amount”, an IntermediaryArrangement “arrangement” and a FormCFiling “filing”, the transaction qualifies for the section 4(a)(6) exemption if—

    (a) (a) Exemption. An issuer may offer or sell securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) of the Securities Act of 1933, provided that:;

    (b) issuer is eligible with issuer;

    (c) offering is within the offering limit with offering;

    (d) investor is within the investment limit with investor and amount;

    (e) intermediary obligations are met with arrangement; and

    (f) disclosure requirements are met with filing and offering.

# Tests

## Fixtures

<!-- l4: decide:a clean issuer -->

**79.** A clean issuer means IssuerProfile where name is Clean Co, organized under, and subject to, the laws of a State or territory of the United States or the District of Columbia is TRUE, subject to the requirement to file reports pursuant to section 13 or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act is FALSE, an investment company, or is excluded from the definition of investment company by section 3(b) or section 3(c) is FALSE, subject to a disqualification as specified in section 227.503(a) is FALSE, has sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) and has not filed the ongoing annual reports required during the two years immediately preceding the filing of the offering statement is FALSE and has no specific business plan, or has indicated that its business plan is to engage in a merger or acquisition with an unidentified company or companies is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a foreign issuer -->

**80.** A foreign issuer means IssuerProfile where name is Ausland GmbH, organized under, and subject to, the laws of a State or territory of the United States or the District of Columbia is FALSE, subject to the requirement to file reports pursuant to section 13 or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act is FALSE, an investment company, or is excluded from the definition of investment company by section 3(b) or section 3(c) is FALSE, subject to a disqualification as specified in section 227.503(a) is FALSE, has sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) and has not filed the ongoing annual reports required during the two years immediately preceding the filing of the offering statement is FALSE and has no specific business plan, or has indicated that its business plan is to engage in a merger or acquisition with an unidentified company or companies is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a delinquent issuer -->

**81.** A delinquent issuer means IssuerProfile where name is Late Filer Inc, organized under, and subject to, the laws of a State or territory of the United States or the District of Columbia is TRUE, subject to the requirement to file reports pursuant to section 13 or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act is FALSE, an investment company, or is excluded from the definition of investment company by section 3(b) or section 3(c) is FALSE, subject to a disqualification as specified in section 227.503(a) is FALSE, has sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) and has not filed the ongoing annual reports required during the two years immediately preceding the filing of the offering statement is TRUE and has no specific business plan, or has indicated that its business plan is to engage in a merger or acquisition with an unidentified company or companies is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a blank-check issuer -->

**82.** A blank-check issuer means IssuerProfile where name is SPAC-ish LLC, organized under, and subject to, the laws of a State or territory of the United States or the District of Columbia is TRUE, subject to the requirement to file reports pursuant to section 13 or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act is FALSE, an investment company, or is excluded from the definition of investment company by section 3(b) or section 3(c) is FALSE, subject to a disqualification as specified in section 227.503(a) is FALSE, has sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) and has not filed the ongoing annual reports required during the two years immediately preceding the filing of the offering statement is FALSE and has no specific business plan, or has indicated that its business plan is to engage in a merger or acquisition with an unidentified company or companies is TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:an offering of -->

**83.** In relation to a NUMBER “prior sales”, a NUMBER “maximum” and a BOOLEAN “previously sold”, an offering of means Offering where target offering amount is maximum, maximum offering amount the issuer will accept is maximum, aggregate amount sold in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months is prior sales and the issuer has previously sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) is previously sold.

<!-- l4: decide:an investor with -->

**84.** In relation to a BOOLEAN “accredited”, a NUMBER “income”, a NUMBER “worth” and a NUMBER “already”, an investor with means InvestorProfile where name is Test Investor, an accredited investor as defined in Rule 501 is accredited, annual income is income, net worth is worth and aggregate amount already sold to this investor across all issuers in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months is already.

<!-- l4: decide:an arrangement with -->

**85.** In relation to a NUMBER “days available” and a NUMBER “intermediaries”, an arrangement with means IntermediaryArrangement where the intermediary complies with section 4A(a) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part is TRUE, the transaction is conducted exclusively through the intermediary's platform is TRUE, the number of intermediaries used for the offering is intermediaries, the intermediary delivered educational materials in connection with establishing the investor's account is TRUE, the intermediary has a reasonable basis for believing that the investor satisfies the investment limitations is TRUE and the days the issuer information has been publicly available on the intermediary's platform before any sale is days available.

<!-- l4: decide:a reporting status with -->

**86.** In relation to a NUMBER “annual reports”, a NUMBER “holders” and a NUMBER “assets”, a reporting status with means ReportingStatus where the issuer is required to file reports under section 13(a) or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act is FALSE, annual reports filed since the most recent sale of securities pursuant to this part is annual reports, holders of record is holders, total assets is assets, the issuer or another party has repurchased all of the securities issued in reliance on section 4(a)(6) is FALSE and the issuer has liquidated or dissolved its business in accordance with state law is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the fixture issuance date -->

**87.** The fixture issuance date means YMD with 2021, 6 and 1.

<!-- l4: decide:a transfer at -->

**88.** In relation to a NUMBER “days since issue” and a BOOLEAN “to accredited”, a transfer at means Transfer where date the securities were issued is the fixture issuance date, date of the transfer is the sum of days since issue and the fixture issuance date, to the issuer of the securities is FALSE, to an accredited investor is to accredited, as part of an offering registered with the Commission is FALSE, to a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent is FALSE, to a trust controlled by the purchaser is FALSE, to a trust created for the benefit of a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent is FALSE, in connection with death of the purchaser is FALSE, in connection with divorce of the purchaser is FALSE and in connection with a circumstance similar to death or divorce of the purchaser is FALSE.

