<!-- l4: decide:a transfer under limb (4) at -->

**96.** In relation to a NUMBER “days since issue”, a BOOLEAN “family”, a BOOLEAN “own trust”, a BOOLEAN “family trust”, a BOOLEAN “death”, a BOOLEAN “divorce” and a BOOLEAN “similar”, a transfer under limb (4) at means Transfer where date the securities were issued is the fixture issuance date, date of the transfer is the sum of days since issue and the fixture issuance date, to the issuer of the securities is FALSE, to an accredited investor is FALSE, as part of an offering registered with the Commission is FALSE, to a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent is family, to a trust controlled by the purchaser is own trust, to a trust created for the benefit of a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent is family trust, in connection with death of the purchaser is death, in connection with divorce of the purchaser is divorce and in connection with a circumstance similar to death or divorce of the purchaser is similar.

## Top level — the whole exemption

<!-- l4: decide:a conforming filing -->

**97.** A conforming filing means FormCFiling where a Form C offering statement was filed with the Commission and provided to investors and the relevant intermediary prior to the commencement of the offering is TRUE, the Form C includes the information required by section 227.201 is TRUE and the financial statements supplied is reviewed.

